<article class="env-remark" id="0B6W">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B6W">Remark <span data-tag="0B6W">48.20.13</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a flat proper morphism of finite type schemes over a pair $(S, \omega _ S^\bullet )$ as in Situation <a href="/tag/0AU4" data-tag="0AU4">48.20.1</a>. The relative dualizing complex (Remark <a href="/tag/0B6S" data-tag="0B6S">48.12.5</a>) is $\omega _{X/Y}^\bullet = a(\mathcal{O}_ Y)$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0AUD" data-tag="0AUD">48.20.8</a> we have the first canonical isomorphism in </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \omega _ X^\bullet = a(\omega _ Y^\bullet ) = Lf^*\omega _ Y^\bullet \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ X}^\mathbf {L} \omega _{X/Y}^\bullet  \]
</div>
  <p> in $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. The second canonical isomorphism follows from the discussion in Remark <a href="/tag/0B6S" data-tag="0B6S">48.12.5</a>. </p>
</article>